      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The paper presents results obtained from a standardized two-stepped survey of 479 males divided into 4 groups: 2 randomized groups of patients aged under 55 years or more, respectively, at the final step of the survey, and 2 hyperlipidemic groups of those of the same age. At the initial and final steps of the survey, the incidence of coronary heart disease (CHD) was analyzed, which varied from 13.5% to 45.6%. It was shown that CHD remission might occur as judged from the epidemiological criteria. The most favorable course of CHD was observed in males with hyperlipidemia at the age of 50-55 years."},
